config ZMK_CLIPBOARD
    bool "Carry what was copied between paired computers"
    depends on ZMK_BLE
    help
      Holds the last text copied on one computer and hands it to the next
      one the keyboard is switched to: to that computer's clipboard if it
      runs the helper, and as typed keystrokes if it does not. Images and
      long text go between two computers that both run the helper.

      The computer that is copied from has to run the helper. The clip is
      kept in RAM only.

if ZMK_CLIPBOARD

config ZMK_CLIPBOARD_MAX_LEN
    int "Longest text clip to hold, in bytes"
    default 16384
    range 64 16384
    help
      Text longer than this is refused, and the keyboard then carries
      nothing rather than a truncated clip. The helpers pass longer text
      between themselves instead, as they do images.

config ZMK_CLIPBOARD_OPAQUE_MAX_LEN
    int "Longest message between helpers to hold, in bytes"
    default 61440
    range 0 65535
    help
      What cannot be typed, an image or a long text, goes from helper to
      helper over the network, and the keyboard only carries the short
      message that says where to fetch it. When the two computers cannot
      reach each other the content itself comes through the keyboard, cut
      down to fit in this many bytes. 0 turns all of that off.

      The larger of this and the text limit is reserved in RAM.

config ZMK_CLIPBOARD_TTL_SEC
    int "Seconds a clip is held before it is wiped"
    default 120
    range 5 3600
    help
      A clip that outlives its usefulness is a liability twice over: it is
      someone's clipboard sitting in a keyboard, and it turns a paste on a
      computer without the helper into typing long after the copy that
      made sense of it.

config ZMK_CLIPBOARD_TYPE_DELAY_MS
    int "Milliseconds between HID reports while typing a clip"
    default 12
    range 2 200
    help
      Each character is two reports, a press and a release. Too short and
      some hosts and remote desktops drop keys.

config ZMK_CLIPBOARD_ACK_WAIT_MS
    int "Milliseconds a paste waits for the helper before typing instead"
    default 700
    range 50 5000

endif # ZMK_CLIPBOARD
